WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.863
Not one sheet of the Duke's gold was wasted.

00:00:03.913 --> 00:00:09.041
So, how can you find the area when the sides use different units?

00:00:09.091 --> 00:00:17.191
Change them to the same unit first, usually the smaller one, like feet to inches or yards to feet.

00:00:17.241 --> 00:00:23.147
Then multiply length times width, and write the area in square units.

00:00:23.197 --> 00:00:31.251
Next time, the Duke wants a panel that uses exactly 48 gold sheets and is 4 inches wide.

00:00:31.301 --> 00:00:33.294
How long must it be?

00:00:33.344 --> 00:00:36.986
That's Area of Rectangles, Part 2.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.402
See you in the workshop.
